    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: derive `ageBand` from `birthDate`\n\nThe endpoint is `POST /api/owners` (OfficeFloor function pipeline), read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`. Following the existing pattern for other derived read-time fields (`locality`, `contactPreference`, `checkDigit`), I made `birthDate` a stored input field and `ageBand` a derived read-time output.\n\n**Edits:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\n   - Added optional `birthDate` (`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema (the create/edit input).\n   - Added read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` response schema. These regenerate `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` on build.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, `birth_date` column) field with getter/setter, so MapStruct persists it in and reads it back out by name.\n\n3. **`function/owner/AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 helper computing the band from `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()`: `<18 \u2192 MINOR`, `18\u201364 \u2192 ADULT`, `\u226565 \u2192 SENIOR`; returns `null` when either date is absent (so owners without a birthDate report no band). Computed against the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`, per the spec.\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `@Mapping(target = \"ageBand\", expression = \"java(AgeBand.of(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`.\n\n5. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added a `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table (tests run under hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema had to carry the column; updated all four for consistency).\n\n**Result:** `AcceptanceTest.coreDerivesAgeBand` (birthDate `1990-01-01`, registered today \u2192 `ADULT`) and the full suite are green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0).",
